// ae3d core: linear algebra, scene types, camera and the backend vtable.
//
// Matrices are column-major and stored flat as m0..m15 with index = col * 4 + row,
// the layout OpenGL and Vulkan both consume without transposition. A Mat4 is
// therefore 16 contiguous doubles, so `&mat` is a valid `const double *` for the
// native uniform and instance-matrix entry points.
//
// Vertex data never crosses into Aether as float32. A model owns a native mesh
// handle (interleaved position/uv/normal, 8 floats per vertex) and, when
// instanced, a native instance handle holding the per-instance matrices. Aether
// drives them through `ae3d.mesh`; the GPU reads them without a conversion pass.
//
// Math, scene and camera types share one module: they reference each other by
// value and every backend needs all three, which is the same grouping gopher3D
// keeps them in.

// The crash handler every program has (it prints the native stack on a
// fault). Declared here, in the module every program imports, so `ae build`
// and `ae run` compile it in; build.sh links it from the engine's shared
// library instead and leaves this copy out.
@source("../../../native/platform/crash.c")

